      "writtenOn": "2024-10-21T15:23:21Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "Right, I need to serialize the access to kvm-\u003earch.pkvm.seqcnt against writers, so using a read lock is one way to do that. And that allows to pull the mt_find() walk below out of the write critical section. Maybe a win, maybe not.\n\nThe alternative I considered was to keep the mt_find() walk into the critical section below, and make kvm-\u003earch.pkvm.seqcnt atomic, so I can just access it lock-free. Wdyt?",
      "parentUuid": "8f34fd32_abb57c7b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1759,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 1759,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "745079a042887713eb8ea215927582425e6134f8",
